@715 = ~Massive Strike~ //No icon and the impossibility to create the effect "next hit"
@716 = ~Massive Strike (Alteration)
Level: 1
Range: 0
Duration: 1 round
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell greatly strengthens the caster's next blow. If it hits, the opponent suffers an additional 1D6 points of damage and must make a successful save vs. breath weapon at -2 or be thrown 10 meters back.~

@717 = ~Fist of Iron~
@718 = ~Fist of Iron (Alteration)
Level: 1
Range: 0
Duration: 5 rounds + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell allows a disarmed warlord to keep fighting. The warlord has to clench his fist while casting this spell, which then becomes as hard as iron. As long as the spell lasts, the mage cannot unclench his fist and cannot hold any weapon, and has a 50% chance of spell failure (he cannot perform the required gestures properly). For most everyday tasks, he must use the other hand.
The Fist of Iron grants +2 to hit and inflicts 1D4 +4 points of damage, but cannot affect creatures that cannot be hurt except by magical weapons. At warlord level 10, the spell improves: the fist counts as a +1 magical weapon, granting +3 to hit and inflicting 1D4 +5 points of damage. From level 15 the spell also improves the caster's unarmed combat skills, granting him an extra attack and +2 to initiative when fighting with the fist of iron.~
@7181 = ~Fist of Iron (Alteration)
Level: 1
Range: 0
Duration: 25 rounds
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell allows a disarmed warlord to keep fighting. The warlord has to clench his fist while casting this spell, which then becomes as hard as iron. As long as the spell lasts, the mage cannot unclench his fist and cannot hold any weapon, and has a 50% chance of spell failure (he cannot perform the required gestures properly). For most everyday tasks, he must use the other hand.
The Fist of Iron counts as a +1 magical weapon, granting +3 to attack rolls and dealing 1D4 +5 points of damage.
The spell also improves the caster's unarmed combat skills, granting him an extra attack and +2 to initiative when fighting with the fist of iron.~
